\f1\b\fs32 \cf0 nv-metapost
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\
nv-metapost is a TeXShop engine for MetaPost and METAFONT files (.mp and .mf). It runs mpost on the file, converts each figure to its own PDF file, and makes a PDF with one figure on each page, which TeXShop shows in the Preview window. When a file writes SVG or PNG figures, the engine makes an HTML file that shows them instead.\
\

\f1\b Installation
\f0\b0 \
Copy the file Engines/nv-metapost.engine in this folder to ~/Library/TeXShop/Engines, then quit and start TeXShop again.\
\

\f1\b Usage
\f0\b0 \
Choose nv-metapost in the engine menu on the toolbar of the source window, or put this line at the top of the file:\
\

\f2 % !TEX TS-program = nv-metapost
\f0 \
\
Then typeset. Lines starting with {\f2 % !MPOST} at the top of the file set options for the engine; for example, {\f2 % !MPOST tex = latex} typesets the text labels with LaTeX. The folder examples has sample files.\
\

\f1\b Requirements
\f0\b0 \
mpost, mptopdf and pdflatex from TeX Live, and the perl that comes with macOS.\
\

\f1\b Known limit
\f0\b0 \
The name of the file must not contain spaces.\
\

